{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1189737-ghoul-family-help","id":1189737,"title":"Ghoul Family Help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-26T18:32:06-08:00","id":1189737,"title":"Ghoul Family Help","content":"So, Ghoul Families are briefly talked about in the Vampire (2E) Core book. Half-Damned touches on them a bit (I hear). Basically, they are Ghouls by birth, instead of made. Age slower, even without vitae, can sense vampires, and the standard ghoul suite. There is also mention of certain deviations from the normal Ghoul capabilities.<br /> <br /> Some questions for potential Ghoul Families:<br /> <br /> Would giving them the ability to invoke the Predatory Aura be a good Gift? Replace one of the Disciplines or no?<br /> <br /> How about alternate Vitae acquisition methods? Eating people? Blood sacrifice?<br /> <br /> Would allowing a proprietary kind of Blood Sorcery as a Discipline work? The ability to use Invictus Oaths or Carthian Law inherently?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T05:28:26-08:00","id":1190212,"title":"","content":"If it fits your game the answer is yes, if you are not the ST you should ask them before trying anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T06:38:54-08:00","id":1190245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1189737-ghoul-family-help?p=1190212#post1190212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it fits your game the answer is yes, if you are not the ST you should ask them before trying anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is for general content (for public consumption/use), so hard rules and consensus is preferred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T12:52:49-08:00","id":1190394,"title":"","content":"I would still be inclined to say yes, if if fits the famlilies backstory then there is no good reason why such a thing couldn't happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T07:48:14-08:00","id":1192258,"title":"","content":"Ghoul family mechanics are, very sadly, left so vague the section might as well have been cut from Half Damned. <br /> <br /> What we do know: you need to determine the creating regent and purpose (accidental or otherwise). Those born as ghouls have an unnatural lifespan (even without Vitae, a born ghoul can live around 150 years), access to Disciplines, and an insatiable hunger for Vitae; family ghouls who do not know they are such suffer from the Unfed Ghoul Conditions on p. 123 of Half Damned. In short, lacking the Vitae results in mental duress, physical degradation, and other malignant Conditions (I suggest Hunger, from the same page).<br /> <br /> Mechanically (p. 105 sidebar), ghoul families<br /> develop and attach Touchstones as vamps do, adding a +2 die bonus<br /> to [Integrity?] breaking point rolls. I... guess this is because they live in a family and live a long time? Not sure why this isn't a broadly available Ghoul Merit, then, or a basic social Merit.<br /> <br /> (<b>Homebrew:</b> <i><b>Family Ties (1 dot)</b>: you live in close proximity to and in relationship with your extended family. This is both a strength to your psyche and a point of conflict; you gain +2 to Integrity Breaking Point rolls but other members of your close family gain +2 to Social rolls against you. If you ever leave or are removed physically from your family and lose a dot of Integrity, you also lose this Merit. Sanctity of Merits applies.)</i><br /> <br /> &quot;The family as a whole also has a benefit and a drawback. Benefits can be Merits, bonuses to Skill Specialties, or access to a certain Discipline. Drawbacks are often, but not always, mental conditions or physical flaws.&quot;<br /> <br /> In practice--by which I mean published materials--the mechanical impact of a &quot;benefit&quot; and a &quot;drawback&quot; vary <b><i><u>extremely widely</u></i></b> from obscure and trivial to OMGWTFBBQ-level of &quot;why can't my ghoul have that?!?&quot; [Immunity to Vinculum I look at thee!] There was also a hinted benefit of &quot;passive Discipline powers active without Vitae&quot;, which would fall into the same category: basically a 5-dot Merit in value.<br /> <br /> And... that's it! That's all we have. So go nuts. There is no published association between the strength of a benefit and a family's drawback as well, but feel free to apply reason. Or don't: supernatural genetic engineering for ubermenchen is a thing.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T09:21:22-08:00","id":1192286,"title":"","content":"One of the reasons I was asking was that I was thinking of developing &quot;other splats/monsters&quot; in Vampire terms.<br /> <br /> So, for &quot;werewolves/lupines&quot;, I was thinking a Ghoul Family that had Protean (for animal transformation into wolves), the ability to get their own Vitae via cannibalism (they can get Vitae from eating the flesh of humans - blood alone isn't enough, but otherwise 1 Vitae per Lethal damage inflicted via bite), and the additional Bane/Drawback of having to deal with Frenzy too.<br /> <br /> For &quot;mages/witches&quot;, a Ghoul Family that had at least one &quot;mental&quot; Discipline (Dominate, Nightmare, Majesty, Obfuscate, Animalism, Auspex) and either a proprietary Blood Sorcery Discipline or access to some Devotions. They could get Vitae on their own via blood sacrifice (ritualized blood-letting, either from themselves or others), and had an additional Bane.<br /> <br /> For &quot;changelings/faeries&quot;, an... oddity. <i>Something</i> abducts people and transforms them into something vaguely Ghoul-like (they aren't undead) that can use Invictus Oaths without needing Invictus Status (and have a few more the Invictus don't - largely because they are of limited use to Kindred). Bane of Iron (or something).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T12:54:11-08:00","id":1192354,"title":"","content":"That... would work fine as a shorthand version of the splats, enabling you to run interactions with just the VtR book. You could, of course, permit these version to purchase additional Disciplines through Merits, within a narrow range. E.g. Resilience and Vigor for lupines, as well as buying up their Disciplines higher than 1 dot. <br /> <br /> Keep in mind that Ghouls are still heavily limited on how high they can take their Disciplines without benefiting from the Vitae of high-BP regents. Breaking that barrier could be a good benefit for a family, IMO.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T12:57:50-08:00","id":1192357,"title":"","content":"Those sound like neat and evocative enough concepts to me that I'd say just do it, even if there isn't precedence in the rule books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"",